 findings were dropped', '4 of the 10 are correct') but no AC names a command/artifact that re-produces or stores the count."],"finding":"The measurement acceptance criteria (AC1 'checked for drops... with a count', AC3 'old prompt's drop rate... measured and recorded in a comment') have no deterministic proving command and their evidence lives in PR/ticket comments, yet they are not tagged [non-codebase]; their done-ness is a human attestation that no step produces as a checkable artifact.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fbcb993b086a33e4c","impact":0.85,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria, lines 1 and 3","norm_id":"n1c30c440641592e7","priority":0.6072,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A reviewer verifying completion cannot run a command to confirm the 145/10/4 counts or the old-prompt drop rate; they must trust prose in a comment."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.7143,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"na","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"na","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"missing_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State the exact verifier model the live replay runs against (matching the gate's deployed `standard` resolution, e.g. the sonnet-4-6 that reproduced the parent's drop) and record the model id with the bounded-run counts, so the test exercises the model where the drop is reproducible rather than one where the old prompt never dropped.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.3111,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan step 2: runs through the gate 'with the gate's settings ... (agentic, `standard` class, temperature 0)' but never pins the model id the `standard` class resolves to under the external tier","Parent ticket doglike-gossipy-pussycat comment: 'On opus-4-8 (the tier default) the agentic arm already spared the findings on the unfixed prompt ... so the defect is model-dependent; it is fully present on the model the gate actually uses' — reproduction required a scratch REBAR_LLM_CONFIG_FILE pinning sonnet-4-6","External tier model resolution is governed by REBAR_LLM_CONFIG_FILE/credentials (tests/external/_live_llm.py, test_pydantic_ai_cutover_live.py), not by the `standard` class name alone"],"finding":"The live replay test's reproducibility of the drop depends on which model the `standard` class resolves to in the external tier, and the parent ticket measured the defect to be model-dependent (opus-4-8 did not drop on the unfixed prompt; only sonnet-4-6 did, via a scratch REBAR_LLM_CONFIG_FILE). The plan does not name the test's target model, so on the tier's default model the test could pass trivially — exercising neither the fix nor a meaningful control margin.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fa61ad708dcf2ae67","impact":0.55,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach step 2 / Testing section / AC 'The live replay test passes on the fixed prompt'","norm_id":"n272374f204db599b","priority":0.4889,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Running the external test on the tier default model where the old prompt never dropped the finding: both the 